1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:05,937
One dream, one wish If you want it,

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,240
gotta go over the top!

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,380
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

6
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,877
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

7
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:41,417
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,180
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

9
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,457
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

10
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:56,420
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

11
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,537
Despite all that to run is not an option.

12
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:01,637
Once they're closed, I
feel the satisfaction.

13
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

14
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,020
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,317
If you are going on your way.

16
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,737
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

18
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,257
Yes, I can.

19
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,057
As you're on your way.

20
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,337
Marks maps will be made.

21
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,197
Yes, with every step that you will take.

22
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

23
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead at new horizons.

24
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,957
In view shining brightly.

25
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:36,860
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you.

26
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:40,137
Dream living, that's the way.

27
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:42,177
Make like a hurricane.

28
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:45,100
Now, got to make your mark today.

29
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,977
One dream, one wish.

30
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

31
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,937
Go for the knockout.

32
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,000
Over the top!

33
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:04,850
Oh!

34
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:08,280
Oh, a secret mission! Okay.

35
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:11,200
So all we need is a plan.

36
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,680
I have a proposal.

37
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,340
In two weeks' time, we
will head to Onigashima.

38
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:21,500
It's an island home to Kaido and
the base of the Beast Pirates.

39
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:23,860
An island? What?

40
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:26,077
You're telling me it's
not on the mainland,

41
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,600
so we have to travel by sea to get to it?

42
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,090
Indeed.

43
00:02:31,173 --> 00:02:32,328
Fortuitously, it's not far.

44
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:36,406
In fact, it's nearly visible from
the land of Wano's shoreline.

45
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:41,100
We will still require a ship,
though not a very large one.

46
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:42,690
Cool.

47
00:02:42,773 --> 00:02:45,772
We'll figure out all those
little details at a later date.

48
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:47,921
When do you need all of us ready?

49
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,494
We have a day in mind.

50
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:53,080
The best time would be the
night of the Fire Festival.

51
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,877
It's a grand celebration for
the people of the capital.

52
00:02:56,960 --> 00:03:00,240
Simply put, Kaido himself
is believed to be a deity.

53
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,320
They think he protects the land,

54
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:07,517
so Orochi will lead the shogun's
procession to pay tribute that day.

55
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,247
But that is merely a facade.

56
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:14,662
What really takes place is a pretentious
banquet for magistrates and beast pirates.

57
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,640
A fine target.

58
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,940
Makes a lot of sense.

59
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,737
So we wait till they get wasted.

60
00:03:20,820 --> 00:03:23,517
Use that to our advantage
and knock those jerks

61
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:26,424
around And then chop the
heads off their leaders

62
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,590
Hey!

63
00:03:27,673 --> 00:03:29,517
I gotta give you a quick warning though,

64
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:34,920
Okiku You'll fall in love after seeing
me kick ass You hear that, sword pervert?

65
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,037
Please calm yourself, Sir Sanji.

66
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,137
Do not be mistaken.

67
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:40,397
I am a perfectly happy married fellow.

68
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:42,257
Okiku is but a comrade of mine.

69
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:44,897
I promise you that there is
no deeper relationship here.

70
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:47,156
Speaking of which, your wife as well?

71
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,630
Huh?

72
00:03:48,713 --> 00:03:49,543
You saw Otsuru?

73
00:03:49,626 --> 00:03:50,456
Indeed

74
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:51,730
Incognito.

75
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:53,770
Splendid.

76
00:03:53,853 --> 00:03:55,265
Good to know she's doing well.

77
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:58,360
But I cannot be selfish
and go see her yet.

78
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:00,380
Not until our work is done.

79
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:01,910
Master Keen.

80
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,310
Stop it!

81
00:04:03,393 --> 00:04:04,440
You're a married man!

82
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:06,346
You can't hog all the ladies!

83
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:09,305
Oh, Kiku, I'm more
deserving of your attention.

84
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,759
Knock it off, you.

85
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:14,540
Hey, Sanji, did you know
Kiku's super strong? Uh-uh.

86
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:19,500
Beautiful and a strong warrior?

87
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:22,120
You're perfect.

88
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:28,757
Now then, I have designed a symbol
to help with getting the word out:

89
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:31,417
two birds of flame to represent time,

90
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:33,877
a habu viper to indicate location,

91
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:36,977
and a reverse crescent moon
which signifies rebellion,

92
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:40,637
twilight—the second hour of
the bird at fire festival.

93
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,297
It shall take place in Habu Port.

94
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:48,500
port If that doesn't make sense, it refers
to the period between 5.30 and 6.00 p .m.

95
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,993
on your foreign clocks.

96
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,560
Don't fret.

97
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:53,333
This is normal in Wano.

98
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,718
They'll understand.

99
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:01,980
We will venture out, distributing
flyers to anyone bearing the mark,

100
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,340
a moon etched on the left ankle.

101
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,219
That is the symbol of insurrection.

102
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,020
They are our allies.

103
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:11,220
There is only one problem.

104
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,657
We don't know how many are out there.

105
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:16,328
But we've taken steps
to maximize our reach.

106
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:20,846
We have comrades spread about
the country getting the word out.

107
00:05:22,020 --> 00:05:26,980
Based at the capital, both Sir Zorojuro
and Sir Usohachi are aiding us.

108
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:31,220
Uh, sorry to say, but I
don't think Zoro's helping.

109
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:37,917
That aside, Sir Furnosuke has disguised
himself as a carpenter's apprentice.

110
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,700
Having located the craftsman
who designed Kaido's mansion,

111
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:44,139
we hope to obtain those blueprints.

112
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,593
They will be essential.

113
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,565
Getting lost is not an option.

114
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:52,520
As for Madam Orobi, she's infiltrated
the walls of Orochi's palace.

115
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:58,020
Vital to our plan, she's keeping tabs on
the Shogun's forces while entertaining him.

116
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:01,400
Rumor has it she's quite popular.

117
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:04,760
Rocking a geisha get up my heart!

118
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:09,066
Now we're together, I wish to
delegate roles to you latecomers.

119
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:14,082
Sir Brook, your ability will be essential
in helping procure food from the capital.

120
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:15,370
It will?

121
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,680
I mean, I guess.

122
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:19,057
Your weather control is like ninjutsu,

123
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:21,260
so you'll be a kunoichi, Madam Nami.

124
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,980
A female ninja?

125
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,720
A kunoichi! Oh, Nami!

126
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,520
I take that.

127
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:29,838
You'll be adorable.

128
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:32,797
Sir Sanji's cooking will
attract attention and

129
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:35,821
also assist us in recruiting
others for our quest.

130
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:37,890
Following?

131
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:39,700
Of course I'll do it.

132
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:40,879
And what about me?

133
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:43,493
You shall be paired up with Sir Chopper.

134
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:47,306
I'd like for you two, along with
Kiku, to join Dogstorm's side.

135
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,900
Cannon, can I dress like a ninja too?

136
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:51,360
Don't see why not?

137
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:56,297
Now that you know your missions, I shall
provide clothes suited for each of you.

138
00:06:56,380 --> 00:07:00,086
Please kindly take these leaves
and place them upon your heads.

139
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,400
Are you ready?

140
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:04,740
Here goes.

141
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,360
Prepare yourselves!

142
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:09,560
Garb-garb-jutsu manifest!

143
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,040
And boom!

144
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,460
Nami, wow!

145
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:23,080
Take a look at you!

146
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:25,900
Yeah! Ninja!

147
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:30,317
You may go about your missions,
since you are in the correct attire.

148
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,400
Hold up, Kin'emon.

149
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,660
This isn't a real ninja outfit.

150
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,700
On the contrary.

151
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,400
That's the ideal look!

152
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,440
I think you're lying to my face!

153
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:45,795
Moving on, allow me to summon
a guide, a real Kunoichi.

154
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:47,310
Come out!

155
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,580
I wonder if she's alive!

156
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:53,400
Can't wait to meet her! Shinobu!

157
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,060
I heed your call.

158
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,940
I knew my outfit was off!

159
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:14,220
What a joke!

160
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:15,880
You bastard!

161
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,120
This is really bad! He's shaking!

162
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:20,574
I think he's in shock!

163
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,680
Kin'emon, you want to explain this to me?

164
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:26,700
The world of Kunoichi is divided in two.

165
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,660
Either sexy or frumpy.

166
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:35,601
If I can pull this up, I'll deal.

167
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,655
Looking good, Brooke.

168
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,357
What are you supposed to be?

169
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:42,620
Well, I assumed I was a man
with panties on his head.

170
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:45,577
But come to think of
it, now I'm not so sure.

171
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:46,490
That's funny.

172
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:53,880
How nice to be so young
and full of spirit.

173
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,500
You all may call me Shinobu.

174
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:59,975
In the past, I was like a
little sister to Master King.

175
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,180
Alas, that was long ago.

176
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:05,840
I specialize in seduction jutsu.

177
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:07,740
Pleasure to meet you.

178
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:12,040
If it weren't for Nami's outfit,
I'd be a broken man right now.

179
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:14,180
Stay with me!

180
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:16,440
Oh, I do understand, young man.

181
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:22,220
Nothing is more deadly
than a mature woman.

182
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:23,970
All right!

183
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:26,857
We shall split up until our
forces are all gathered.

184
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:30,469
Take note of three samurai in
particular we hope to recruit.

185
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:34,080
Finding them will be a tremendous help.

186
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:38,840
They are Kawamatsu,
Ashida Doji, and Denjiro.

187
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:43,300
Much like your present company,
they too once served Lord Odin.

188
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:46,140
It's time.

189
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:48,500
Best of luck with your objectives.

190
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:52,700
We are closing in on our wretched targets.

191
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,720
The Shogun Orochi and Kaido 2.

192
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,217
The fire festivals in two weeks.

193
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:00,200
That's the execution date.

194
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:07,260
We'll storm Kaido's base on Onigashima and
return this nation to its former glory!

195
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:38,900
Oh, my God.

196
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,560
Well, hello.

197
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:03,700
Take it all.

198
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,480
You can't keep the good stuff to yourself.

199
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:10,517
You got to share.

200
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,430
Give it back.

201
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:13,248
Luffy Toto brought us that.

202
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:16,780
We may never see riches like
this again. I don't care.

203
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,170
Oh, Mama.

204
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:19,490
Huh?

205
00:11:19,573 --> 00:11:20,960
They've got sake, too.

206
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:22,060
This is fancy.

207
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:23,320
Awful greedy.

208
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:24,680
How could you?

209
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,700
My grandson is so hungry.

210
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:29,140
Shut your trap!

211
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,380
Just die already!

212
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,430
Huh?

213
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,310
Move!

214
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,060
Somebody's got a fat head.

215
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:46,046
Who the hell would pull
off a heist like this?

216
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,640
Acting like some hero and
giving food to the poor?

217
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:52,848
They're selling you
hope when there is none.

218
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,977
You get your food, then
you lose it just as fast.

219
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:59,320
Slipping through your fingers
like it was just a dream.

220
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:03,597
There's no samurai here who will
stand up for the downtrodden.

221
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:05,280
They all lost their spines.

222
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,777
There's no one left to lead them either.

223
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:12,737
No men with honor or
conviction or an ounce of guts.

224
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:16,080
There's no one left to
keep this ship on course.

225
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:20,380
The land of Wano is finished.

226
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:23,200
You all know it.

227
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:28,520
Hear that, you old hag?

228
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,957
You're holding on to
life for no damn reason.

229
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:35,200
All you're gonna see is more
suffering and more senseless cruelty!

230
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:45,260
Should I put you out of your misery?

231
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,780
Please run! Grandma!

232
00:12:57,140 --> 00:13:01,720
I believe in Lady Odoki's
words, and I always will.

233
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:04,770
Ha!

234
00:13:04,853 --> 00:13:06,000
She's long dead.

235
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:09,340
The nine samurai will return to this land,

236
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:13,940
and Lord Odin's dream will
surely be fulfilled. Yeah? How?

237
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:16,140
Who could take Odin's place?

238
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,420
Who could lead their revolt?

239
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:30,790
Shitenmaru!

240
00:13:30,873 --> 00:13:32,500
Sir, this is bad! No!

241
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:52,390
No!

242
00:13:52,473 --> 00:13:54,640
So, we meet at last.

243
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:02,960
The head of the Thieves Brigade. Whoa!

244
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,180
That thing's a monster!

245
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:10,500
A pirate named Straw Hat Luffy came
around here recently. Seen anything?

246
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:17,700
If I tell you I don't know him,
will you turn around and leave?

247
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:19,075
Because I doubt that.

248
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,560
Watch your tongue, thief.

249
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,417
You're lucky,

250
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:28,657
Kaido wants you as part
of his crew because if it

251
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:32,057
was up to me I would have
stomped you out long ago,

252
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:37,140
so if you think I owed you even an
ounce of respect, you're mistaken.

253
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:43,360
All right, if you hate me so much!

254
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,220
But I've only got one answer for you!

255
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,617
Real quick, Kin'emon,

256
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:03,397
I understand your strategy so far but
there's one thing I'm still confused about.

257
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,697
Odin brought down Ashura
Doji 20 years ago.

258
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:11,917
All right, but you also said he's
the one samurai we need to find.

259
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,177
He fought Odin but he's loyal to him.

260
00:15:14,260 --> 00:15:17,140
A fair question to ask, I'd say.

261
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,297
It's quite simple.

262
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:24,560
Ashida Doji was defeated,
then mended his ways.

263
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:28,057
He pledged loyalty to Lord
Odin when he saw his worth.

264
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:29,477
But now...

265
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,500
It seems that he's doing
wicked deeds once more.

266
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,357
Shutenmaru, he's called.

267
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:37,480
He's the leader of the
Atamayama Thieves Brigade.

268
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:42,100
I swear I've heard that name.

269
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,660
I got a question.

270
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,520
Is he really strong?

271
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:50,290
Indeed.

272
00:15:50,373 --> 00:15:51,203
Have no doubt.

273
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:54,700
In fact, he may be the
strongest samurai of all.

274
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,240
I'm ready.

275
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,660
Hey, shit!

276
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:26,860
Samurai aren't so weak.

277
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:36,360
Master Jack!

278
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,760
If it's your way.

279
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:21,980
Back away!

280
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:24,220
Master Jack is letting loose!

281
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:26,009
This is going to get ugly!

282
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,740
We're all doomed, aren't we?

283
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,320
No!

284
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:16,900
Ever since he died, I've
lost any reason to fight.

285
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:21,180
I've long since been ready to follow him.

286
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:29,170
However...

287
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:33,900
Getting killed by an underling
like you is not the answer!

288
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:36,280
Cut the crap!

289
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:51,577
I should have died

290
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:56,997
together with living

291
00:18:57,080 --> 00:19:03,680
is suffering I'm so sick of it all

292
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,480
Ahhhh! Yeah!

293
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:21,620
Ahhhh!

294
00:19:23,820 --> 00:19:25,220
Ahhhh!

295
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:26,670
Ahhhh!

296
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:46,720
Master Jack!

297
00:19:47,660 --> 00:19:49,980
The sky! Look up!

298
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:54,760
Oh boy!

299
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:58,737
He came in person.

300
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:01,180
What could kind of be plotting?

301
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:10,437
Those clouds came out of
nowhere—guess it's gonna rain!

302
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:12,517
It's him!

303
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,477
Hey, Straw Hat, get over here!

304
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,390
here

305
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:18,200
I'm coming. What's up?

306
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:21,900
What the hell?

307
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,720
Lord Momonosuke! What?

308
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:39,660
Lord Momonosuke has changed.

309
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,040
He's a dragon?

310
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:45,297
I will explain the details
later, but this is no illusion.

311
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:47,340
His body can change forms.

312
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:52,420
Of all cursed things, the
poor boy has become a dragon!

313
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,240
This is bad.

314
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:58,300
Really bad.

315
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:10,500
Run! Run away!

316
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:15,200
What does he want?

317
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:16,680
Why now?

318
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,420
Hey, Jack.

319
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:30,420
Yes, sir.

320
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:36,560
Find those punks and bring them here.

321
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:39,720
Step on it or else.

322
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:44,020
Whoa!

323
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:45,520
What is that?

324
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:48,180
This couldn't get any worse.

325
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:51,200
That dragon...

326
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:54,580
is Kaido.

327
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:57,920
So that's him.

328
00:21:58,840 --> 00:21:59,880
Kaido.

329
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:39,160
Wait, Kaido was a dragon?

330
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:41,700
Yes.

331
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:51,220
This is the opponent that we face.

332
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:00,080
A brutal warrior.

333
00:23:03,020 --> 00:23:06,080
Who can transform into a beast.

334
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:17,520
Is he going in to Okapore?

335
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:22,367
I wonder, what could have brought
him to Kuma all of a sudden?

336
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:25,977
Sorry, Kin'emon.

337
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:27,857
We were identified by them.

338
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:30,500
Me, Straw Hat, and Zoro as well. You what?

339
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,717
But they only know that
we're here in Wano.

340
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,597
They don't know about the plan.

341
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:38,437
Is that supposed to be reassuring?

342
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:40,344
How'd you screw this up so bad?

343
00:23:41,300 --> 00:23:44,237
You Straw Hats can't stick
to a plan to save your lives.

344
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:46,379
I don't have to take that from you.

345
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:49,562
It was Luffy's fault, wasn't it?

346
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:51,360
I'm sorry, Law. Again.

347
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:57,200
So given the timing, Kaido's probably
looking for me and Straw Hats.

348
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:02,557
The Beast Pirates have an
overwhelming presence here thanks to

349
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:06,228
two key resources they put all
their strength into producing.

350
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:12,507
First, there are the weapons that Kaido
is forcing the citizens to manufacture.

351
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:17,500
Second, there are the smiles
Kaido uses to fortify his troops.

352
00:24:18,220 --> 00:24:22,220
These are the artificial devil
fruits made by Caesar and Doflamingo.

353
00:24:23,260 --> 00:24:26,520
But, as you know, we cut
that off at the source.

354
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:30,637
After capturing Caesar and
destroying his lab on Punk Hazard,

355
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:33,308
any further smile
development was shut down.

356
00:24:37,340 --> 00:24:42,757
after that we destroyed doflamingo's
factory and dress rosa this

357
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:48,437
shut down production and trade
distribution of smile in no time now

358
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:52,157
kaido's business partner is not
only dethroned but locked in prison

359
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:59,160
so in the simplest terms possible
we picked a fight with kaido

360
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,397
The Samurai aren't even on his radar.

361
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:05,540
He's just after me and Straw Hat.

362
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:11,040
Hey! Luffy!

363
00:25:11,400 --> 00:25:13,660
Where are you going? Sir Luffy!

364
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:15,940
Stay here! Let me go!

365
00:25:17,260 --> 00:25:18,897
They know about the two of us,

366
00:25:18,980 --> 00:25:21,697
but they don't know that the
rest of our crews are here.

367
00:25:21,780 --> 00:25:24,839
You need to stay out of
sight to keep that a secret.

368
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:29,842
Otherwise, they'll hunt us down.

369
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:38,380
This is obviously bad, but
let's work with what we've got.

370
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:40,849
Hawkins doesn't know much.

371
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:49,880
Continue with your plan.

372
00:25:51,220 --> 00:25:52,050
Understand?

373
00:25:52,133 --> 00:25:54,657
All right, but what about you two?

374
00:25:54,740 --> 00:25:59,157
I wish I could let things be,

375
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:04,180
but Straw Hat's already gotten involved
with the people of this country.

376
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:16,820
If he can't control his
emotions, our plan will fail!

377
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:22,230
them.

378
00:26:22,313 --> 00:26:24,460
We need the entire alliance with us.

379
00:26:24,660 --> 00:26:26,537
That is the only way we can succeed.

380
00:26:26,620 --> 00:26:27,500
I can

381
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:35,957
pull this together somehow.

382
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:36,870
Now, room.

383
00:26:36,953 --> 00:26:39,077
In the meantime, stay out of sight.

384
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,380
It shambles.

385
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:43,060
Be careful!

386
00:26:51,900 --> 00:26:53,077
Damn it, Luffy.

387
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:55,900
We weren't apart that
long. What did you do?

388
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:15,017
Thieves Brigade, retreat to the forest!

389
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:17,980
We don't want to get in a tussle with him!

390
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:37,640
I've heard many a tale, you know,

391
00:27:38,100 --> 00:27:42,860
of the mighty brigandous underlings
living deep in the mountains of Khuri.

392
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:54,020
You may have changed your
name, but I remember you.

393
00:28:17,340 --> 00:28:19,620
That's all in the past, though, right?

394
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:25,140
Just bow down to me, buddy.

395
00:28:36,300 --> 00:28:39,940
I'd be happy to wipe the
slate clean between us.

396
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,780
Whoa, that stinks!

397
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:10,400
Kaido, don't tell me you're drunk!

398
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:11,750
Hmm?

399
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:13,680
What do you mean, Big Dummy?

400
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,500
Of course not.

401
00:29:16,660 --> 00:29:18,280
He's super drunk!

402
00:29:28,040 --> 00:29:30,960
What's it gonna be, Shetemura?

403
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:33,300
We can't run!

404
00:29:33,580 --> 00:29:35,404
I'll have to create an opening!

405
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:43,717
I'm trying to stop the bleeding!

406
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,153
Please don't move, sir!

407
00:29:45,300 --> 00:29:47,137
Yeah, but Commander Kaido is wasted.

408
00:29:47,220 --> 00:29:49,597
There's no telling how
much damage he might do.

409
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:52,717
You're saying we gotta get
out of here or we're all dead?

410
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:54,640
That's a possibility, yeah.

411
00:29:55,320 --> 00:29:58,026
I'm worried about the
people of Okamori Tower.

412
00:29:58,180 --> 00:30:00,415
We need them to work in the factories.

413
00:30:01,420 --> 00:30:04,080
It's fine if Kaido
wants to set an example,

414
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:06,817
but he can't just wreak
havoc all over Kuri.

415
00:30:06,900 --> 00:30:08,860
He's gonna wipe out his own men.

416
00:30:09,620 --> 00:30:12,317
You didn't think to share
that important detail with me?

417
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:13,230
Really?

418
00:30:13,500 --> 00:30:15,080
Forgive me, Master Keen.

419
00:30:15,540 --> 00:30:17,187
You return to Odin's palace.

420
00:30:17,560 --> 00:30:19,800
Allow me to rescue Saru. Please.

421
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:21,660
I'm responsible as well.

422
00:30:23,220 --> 00:30:24,220
Really, woman?

423
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:27,598
You should have taken another
husband to protect you.

424
00:30:28,040 --> 00:30:29,280
Twenty long years.

425
00:30:29,580 --> 00:30:31,874
You waited all this time for my return?

426
00:30:32,260 --> 00:30:35,260
Saru, I shall make you wait no longer.

427
00:30:39,280 --> 00:30:41,540
Damn, it's still a long way.

428
00:30:42,740 --> 00:30:44,317
Right behind you, Straw Hats.

429
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:48,020
Hey, Traffy, you think the
people of Okoborre Town are okay?

430
00:30:48,320 --> 00:30:52,297
They'd be a hell of a lot better if
some pirate didn't decide to play hero.

431
00:30:52,380 --> 00:30:53,917
Mind your own business next time.

432
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:56,412
But it's us Kaido wants, not them, right?

433
00:30:56,500 --> 00:30:57,330
It's gotta be.

434
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:21,560
Supreme Commander, sir!

435
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:24,420
Is it he?

436
00:31:24,780 --> 00:31:26,420
One of the headliners?

437
00:31:27,460 --> 00:31:32,166
Commander, I assume that you're searching
for Straw Hat Luffy and Trafalgar Law.

438
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:35,637
I have found them.

439
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:38,544
They're tucked away in
the ruins of Odin Castle.

440
00:31:40,660 --> 00:31:41,700
Baton Kasseler.

441
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:51,190
Hawkers...

442
00:31:51,273 --> 00:31:52,240
Is that true?

443
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:56,598
They've been hiding in those ruins
under our noses and we didn't know!

444
00:31:56,800 --> 00:31:57,720
It's a lie.

445
00:31:58,120 --> 00:32:01,860
I said it is a means of redirecting
his rampage. For a time.

446
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:05,814
However, this should work to our favor.

447
00:32:06,900 --> 00:32:09,497
there is an old legend
attached to that castle

448
00:32:09,580 --> 00:32:12,797
and because of it people
are claiming that they've

449
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:16,817
seen an eerie light there
they still believe that

450
00:32:16,900 --> 00:32:20,197
that the kozuki samurai
will come back for revenge

451
00:32:20,280 --> 00:32:23,817
from beyond the grave just
in time for the anniversary

452
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:27,157
huh indeed which i'm
certain has become a great

453
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:30,477
cause of stress for the
shogun so destroying that

454
00:32:30,560 --> 00:32:33,384
castle would kill two
birds with with one stone.

455
00:32:38,340 --> 00:32:41,100
Old Odin castle, huh?

456
00:32:53,420 --> 00:32:55,460
That brings back memories.

457
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:58,420
It's a fine hiding place indeed.

458
00:32:59,240 --> 00:33:00,720
But not anymore.

459
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:09,137
You're thinking punks can get
away with what you've done.

460
00:33:09,220 --> 00:33:13,080
Taking my smile fruits away didn't stop.

461
00:33:14,780 --> 00:33:17,260
You awoke by wrath.

462
00:33:21,980 --> 00:33:26,160
What the hell, why is he
going toward the castle?

463
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,400
Hey, guys.

464
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:48,960
Oh, is it just me or is
he coming straight for us?

465
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:50,520
I think you're right.

466
00:33:52,120 --> 00:33:54,980
But how did he notice
I was from so far away?

467
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:57,500
Oh, no.

468
00:33:58,400 --> 00:34:00,300
Maybe he's just making a circle.

469
00:34:03,860 --> 00:34:04,760
No.

470
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:07,740
He knows.

471
00:34:14,020 --> 00:34:15,760
Run! Hurry!

472
00:34:24,420 --> 00:34:26,832
Why is he headed straight for the castle?

473
00:34:58,300 --> 00:34:59,400
It can't be.

474
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:15,760
Oh, no! Not that!

475
00:35:30,580 --> 00:35:31,840
Run for it!

476
00:35:32,420 --> 00:35:33,360
Shut up!

477
00:35:35,280 --> 00:35:36,960
Last breath!

478
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,640
Captain, help!

479
00:36:53,460 --> 00:36:56,260
Oh, my God.

480
00:37:10,980 --> 00:37:12,380
Kaido!
